.nh
.TH "PB-DOMAIN" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-domain - Add your own domains to the workspace


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb domain [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a domain you control (example.com or dev.example.com) once. After its DNS records
are in place and it shows verified, any name one level under it (app.example.com) can be used by
tunnels and previews with --domain, with HTTPS from one shared certificate.

.PP
Add domains you control to the active workspace once, then use any name one level under a verified domain for tunnels and previews (--domain). Team domains are added and removed by owners and admins.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for domain


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP, \fBpb-domain-add(1)\fP, \fBpb-domain-list(1)\fP, \fBpb-domain-remove(1)\fP, \fBpb-domain-show(1)\fP, \fBpb-domain-verify(1)\fP
